      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is proud to present no.5 Glendale, a distinctive detached home full of character and flair- one of just eight 4 bedroom homes built by the Woods Group in 2016 in this peaceful enclave set within the Old Nurseries.\nBuilt within the wonderfully mature grounds of a demolished mid- Century residence whose treescape boundaries provide a haven of calm and quiet around a fine amenity green, no5 Glendale is within minutes' walk of Delgany village, while also being convenient to Greystones' many attractions. \n\nFortunate enough to reserve No5 during the early construction phase, the owners' designer collaborated with the house-builder to subtly adapt the interior layout and enhance the ground floor accommodation. The home features an impressive open plan ground floor layout, while the owners took great pride in creating a home that blends style with a touch of luxury and is now presented to the market in showhouse-like condition. \n\nThere is high quality tiling throughout the ground floor; a beautiful bespoke kitchen by Andrew Ryan of Wexford featuring extensive display cabinetry; contemporary glass-balustrade stairs to the first floor gallery landing; tastefully appointed bathrooms; and a spectacular orangery-styled conservatory that opens directly into the lusciously planted rear garden which was designed and executed to be a \"room outside\" by Exhibition Landscapes' Johnathan Wallis and features several specimen varieties such as Japanese Maple, cherry blossom, Wisteria, roses and ferns among others, that have matured beautifully and are awash with colour no matter the season. \n \nA hall porch opens into a well-proportioned living room spanning the entire width of the house, where a log-effect enclosed gas fire set in a matt stone fireplace surround is the welcoming focal point. Glazed double doors invite one along into the spacious quality handcrafted kitchen with its central breakfast island, pausing for a moment in the dining room before reaching the fine conservatory.\n\nOn the first floor, the front ensuite principal bedroom is beautifully proportioned and enjoys a southerly aspect where the box-bay window, complete with window-seat, affords views to the pine trees on the Farrankelly skyline. Opposite the grey marble-themed family bathroom, the second and third bedrooms intercommunicate to form a versatile combination of nursery bedroom/dressing room or visiting family guest suite. The layout of these rooms could easily be reconfigured to provide two separate spaces once again. The entire top floor comprises another large ensuite bedroom with library shelving and wall-to-wall fitted workstation ideal for study or remote / homeworking.\n\nGlendale is accessed by car from Convent Road via the Old Nurseries, and a pedestrian walkway through to Delgany Wood lends ready access to Killincarrig on the R761 coast road. Every convenience of modern living is on hand in this popular location, with local retail and hospitality options in charming Delgany village being less than 10 minutes on foot, while just a few minutes away by car from Greystones village. Local schools within striking distance include Delgany National School, St Laurence's Primary School and secondary options at Templecarrig, St Davids and Greystones Community College are a short distance away. \n\nDay to day living could not be any easier with a range of first class shopping and dining options close at hand. Commuters will appreciate the proximity to the Dart Station in Greystones, with a park and ride available in the village. An enviable array of sporting and leisure facilities for adults and children alike are close at hand, including several renowned golf clubs but a few minutes away. Tennis, rugby, soccer, GAA, lawn bowls, paddle, swimming, sailing, fishing - it's all here for you to enjoy. \n\nViewing is by prior appointment and can be arranged through the MySherryFitz app or calling the Greystones office on (01) 2874005."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGlazed Hall Porch - \nWith mosaic tiled floor and radiator cabinet. Glazed screen door to:\n\nSitting Room - 5.89m x 7.24m\nWith tiled floor, featuring a stairwell with glazed balustrade, ascending to first floor gallery landing. A deep box bay window affords a wonderful sense of light against the backdrop of mature amenity green boundary trees. Radiator cabinet, picture lighting and recessed downlighters. Log-effect enclosed gas fire set in matt stone fireplace surround, mantlepiece and hearth. Glazed double doors to:\n\nKitchen/ Dining Room - 5.89m x 6.04m\nBespoke handcrafted cabinetry by Andrew Ryan of Wexford, with integrated Siemens appliances, featuring an impressive central quartz-topped breakfast island incorporating generous undercounter retracting drawers, integrated dishwasher, and recycling/bin compartment. A matching worktop and splashback complement a four-plate electric induction hob two gas rings beneath an extractor canopy with downlighters. A double-oven electric cooker with integrated grill and microwave functions sits atop a plate-warming drawer, and the deep stainless-steel sink is equipped with a Quooker boiling-water tap. There is extensive utensil drawer capacity with crafted solid oak dividing compartments. A double-fronted oak-shelved larder is located beside the integrated fridge and freezer.The dining area beyond the kitchen is pleasantly down-lit by twin electronically controlled Velux rooflights, and its two discreetly up-lit alcoves have been fitted with attractive glazed display cabinets with lighting, above deep pull-out drawers.This area segues seamlessly to the orangery-style sunroom.\n\nConservatory - 5.89m x 5.54m\nBathed in day-long light, this spectacular room with pelmet-lights, ceiling fan, and two pairs of double doors leading to the rear garden is such a versatile space to be enjoyed all year round by family and friends- a perfect place to gather or for entertaining on special occasions where the rear garden also becomes a room outside in favourable weather as the sun shines.\n\nRear Hall - \nFitted cupboard and Dyson docking point/charger.\n\nGuest WC - \nWith WC, vanity mirror over wash basin and locker, feature tiled wall. Mechanical extract fan.\n\nUtility Room - \nWith washing machine and condenser clothes-dryer. Cloaks cupboard. Door to gated side entrance.\n\nUpstairs: - \nFirst floor gallery landing with southerly aspect; picture lights and bracket wall lights.\n\nPrincipal Bedroom 1 - 3.92m x 5.35m\nFacing south, featuring wall-to-wall mirror-fronted wardrobes, and a charming window-seat with linen-drawers beneath. Bracket wall-lights and recessed downlighters.\n\nEnsuite - 3.47m x 1.78m\nFully tiled, with glazed shelving, corner wall-cabinet, mirrored cabinet over wash basin. W.C. Shower with rainfall head and hand-held fitting. Mechanical extract fan.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.47m x 3.72m\nRadiator cabinet; glazed double doors intercommunicate with:\n\nBedroom 3/Dressing Room - 2.42m x 2.55m\nExtensively furnished as luxury dressing room complete with mirror-fronted double wardrobe, drawers, and generous shelving and clothes-hanging.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nThemed in grey marble tiling; down-lit vanity wall mirror above wash basin and locker; WC, glazed screen shower with rainfall head and hand-held fitting.\n\nA second flight of stairs from the gallery landing accesses the top floor landing, and: - \n\n\nBedroom 4/Home Office - 4.57m x 6.13m\nThis large bright room spans the entire attic and enjoys lovely afternoon and evening sun via its Velux and gable window combination. Double wardrobe, library shelving, workstation desk with extensive undercounter cupboards and drawers.\n\nEnsuite - 2.29m x 1.91m\nFully tiled, with Velux roof light, WC. mirrored wall cabinet above wash basin and locker, glazed screen tiled shower with wall niche, rainfall head and hand-held fitting. Mechanical extract fan.\n\nOutside - \nThe front garden with established hedges on either side has paved parking for two vehicles, and a pebble bed whose planting includes camelia and an olive tree.Gated side entrances hold storage lockers and access the rear garden where Jonathan Wallis designed a low-maintenance setting with sandstone terrace paving complemented by low plinths to each side with bamboo side screening and a crescent shaped stone clad retaining wall supporting an alpine bank stocked with a luscious plant selection including several specimen varieties such as Japanese Maple/acers, cherry blossom, \" bottlebrush\", Wisteria, roses and ferns. There are external power points, garden lighting, and a water feature; all against a rear boundary hedge over which a white-thorn faithfully blooms each spring.\n\n"
      },
